<title>ECUADOR: Ecuador's coffee exports fell 34.2 pct in Jan.</title>
<headline>Ecuador's coffee exports fell 34.2 pct in Jan.</headline>
<dateline>QUITO 1997-02-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ecuador's coffee exports fell 34.2 percent in January to 51,056 60-kg bags due to the retention plan of the Association of Coffee Producing Countries (ACPC), an exporters group said Friday.</p>
<p>The National Coffee Exporter Association said Ecuador shipped 77,592 bags in January 1996.</p>
<p>Meanwhile, coffee revenues fell 51.1 percent in January to $3.87 million from $7.92 million in January 1996.</p>
<p>Ecuador plans to export 1.4 million bags between July 1996 and June 1997.</p>
<p>Coffee is Ecuador's fifth export earner, after oil, banana, shrimp and cacao.</p>
<p>((--Gustavo Oviedo, Quito Newsroom, 5932 258433))</p>
</text>
